Hi all,

I am new to using N-mixture models using the unmarked package. I am trying to estimate abundance and detection probabilities for bird species surveyed across three years at 35 different point count stations within two treatments. In each year, I conducted 5 visits to each point count station. I just looked at Western Meadowlark abundance and detection probability, but both seemed abnormally low. I am using the pcount function to fit a model. My encounter data (below code) includes Visits 1-5=2015, Visits 6-10=2016, Visits 11-15=2017, but does not have the site column because it is set up as the "y" data frame for unmarkedFramePCount. I saw a previous post someone had on this topic, but it didn't seem to apply to my data. The code I used follows:

WEMEy<-read.csv("yWEME.csv")

