hi Kate,
 you should read this : http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ecy.2093/full
 and maybe a couple related papers cited by Marc Kery and try to answer that question for yourself.  The short answer is that choice of K should be chosen large enough so that it doesn't have an effect on the result.... if it does then you should reconsider the problem and possibly chose an alternative analysis framework.
regards
andy

